# Ignored wholesale EXCEPT output/raw_runs/, whose small text products are
# tracked -- see the CASCADE run outputs block at the bottom of this file.
output/*
!output/raw_runs/

# joint_fit.json is the ONLY thing under output/ that is an INPUT rather than a
# product: HAT_run_all.py stage 6 reads it and passes its (M, f) to every groin
# run in the matrix. Untracked, the calibrated pair lived on one machine only --
# a clone had no groin parameters at all, and the values existed solely in
# commit messages. Tracked, the pin travels with the repository.
# The directory is re-included and then re-excluded so ONLY this file returns;
# the sweep cells and figures beside it stay ignored.
!output/groin_sweep/
output/groin_sweep/*
!output/groin_sweep/joint_fit.json

# output/comparisons/ (one rule since 2026-09-17; before that a per-folder
# whitelist for smoothing_vs_cascade, then rate_windows): every README,
# CAPTIONS.md, .csv and .txt in the tree is tracked -- the tables a results
# document quotes, the report.txt that names the runs a set read, and
# runs_used.csv / y_bounds.txt -- so the numbers survive a clone. Images,
# PDFs, GIFs and .npz are regenerable from those plus the code and stay
# ignored. Directories are re-included so the patterns can reach into the
# nested figure folders (coastsat/means, sensitivity/ends-swapped/duneline/lrr,
# relocation/1984_2004/v2/calibBE_groin/tables, ...).
!output/comparisons/
output/comparisons/**
!output/comparisons/**/
!output/comparisons/**/README.md
!output/comparisons/**/CAPTIONS.md
!output/comparisons/**/*.csv
!output/comparisons/**/*.txt

