# raw/cached data under data/hatteras_init/
#
# 1-barrier3d-domains holds ~160 MB of .npy topography arrays, so its CONTENTS
# are ignored -- but the written record of what is in there, and of what has
# been deleted from it, is not. Those files are the only account of several
# irreversible purges (the arrays were never tracked, so git cannot recover
# them) and they were themselves ignored until 2026-09-03.
#
# Written as `/**` rather than `/`: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT
# DIRECTORY is excluded, so a plain directory rule makes every negation below
# silently do nothing. The `!**/` line re-includes directories only, so git can
# descend far enough to see the files named after it.
data/hatteras_init/1-barrier3d-domains/**
!data/hatteras_init/1-barrier3d-domains/**/
!data/hatteras_init/1-barrier3d-domains/**/README.md
!data/hatteras_init/1-barrier3d-domains/LINEAGE.md
!data/hatteras_init/1-barrier3d-domains/archive_purge_*.csv
# The dune-line shift measurements. Small, and NOT regenerable from this repo
# alone -- HAT_measure_duneline_shift.py needs the D: GIS drive and a topography
# version to measure against. duneline_retreat_1984_1997.csv in particular is
# where N comes from for every seaward-row insert version.
!data/hatteras_init/1-barrier3d-domains/**/duneline-shift/*.csv
data/hatteras_init/3-env-forcings/water_level/noaa_cache_8651370/
data/hatteras_init/3-env-forcings/storms/WIS_raw_data/
data/hatteras_init/3-env-forcings/storms/old/
data/hatteras_init/4-mgmt-forcing/road_offset/raster/
data/hatteras_init/5-scr/1-observations/coastsat_timeseries/
# The 5-scr geojsons (the 80 MB CoastSat transect layer, nc_shorelines at
# 20 MB, the study-area and wet/dry lines) stay on disk but off GitHub
# (Hannah, 2026-09-18). They were untracked when 5-scr was regrouped into
# 1-observations/ .. 4-comparisons/; the copies already in history remain
# there. A clone does NOT get them: the scripts that read them need a copy
# from someone who has one.
data/hatteras_init/5-scr/**/*.geojson
# Same decision for 4-mgmt-forcing (Hannah, 2026-09-18): the two NC-12 lines
# (raw_offset/1978, /2008) and the relocation sample points stay on disk, off
# GitHub. The line files are INPUTS -- the setback producer, the relocation
# measurement and several figures read them through
# hat_topo_version.road_line_file() -- so a clone cannot rebuild the setbacks
# or redraw those figures without a copy from someone who has one.
data/hatteras_init/4-mgmt-forcing/**/*.geojson

